 "note": "AM run. Checked 75 people and filed 9 bullets across 7 people, each verified on its source page by the parent and read back in the Sheet exactly once. Fresh sweep: the dedicated sweep of the Oct 24 to Nov 14 window found no new winner \u2014 its two directory hits (Michelle Johnston's Shaffer Award and Kwadwo Appiah-Kubi's tenure) are already on file \u2014 but the rotation checks surfaced two fresh winners from Clarkson's Nov 13 game against Yale: Janelle Evans won the faceoff that set up the game-winning goal, and Raedyn Spademan scored the tying goal on a redirect (Clarkson University Athletics, published Nov 13, 2026); both filed fresh. Also filed: Jordyn Hill's opening-match loss by fall at the Nov 2025 state collegiate wrestling championships; Kaitlyn Mallette's two freshman-season assists (Brown, Nov 2025, and Saint Michael's, Jan 2026) and her 2025 graduation from George Elliott Secondary School; Victoria Fitch leading SUNY Potsdam's Reunion 2026 online campus tour; and Conor Miller-Lynch's poster and final report at the CITeR Fall 2026 Program Review in Charlotte. CORRECTION MERGED: Ana Miller's record says she began a leave of absence from her Madison Elementary special-education role in Feb 2026, running through Feb 2027; Massena Central's 2026-27 employee directory lists her as Teacher - Integrated Pre-K at Madison Elementary, so the listing was filed as it reads, without claiming she has returned from leave, and her blank Companies field was filled with Massena Central School District. Logged, not filed: Toni Squires is still listed as an absent member at SUNY Canton's Feb 10, 2026 College Council meeting while the council page says her term expired in 2025 \u2014 one attendance line split across two pages is not enough to file a term change; a SUNY Potsdam caption from the Shusda Classroom dedication gives Victoria Fitch's class year as '24 against the '23 on her record and shows no year for the ceremony, so it was left alone. 3 candidates ad